# design-slop-lint per-repo exceptions
#
# One label per line. A label here suppresses that check for THIS repo only.
# Every entry needs a justification, because an unexplained entry is
# indistinguishable from disabling the gate.

# The three linear-gradient uses in client/src/index.css are all SINGLE-HUE GOLD:
#   .text-gradient-gold      gold -> deeper gold on the hero key phrase
#   .editorial-divider       w-16 h-px, gold -> transparent
#   .editorial-divider-center w-24 h-px, transparent -> gold -> transparent
#
# The banned tell is a multi-hue gradient (the purple-to-blue surface fill) used
# as decoration. A 1px rule that fades to transparent is a hairline, not a
# gradient fill, and single-hue gold is the brand accent defined in
# docs/DESIGN-DOCTRINE.md. Reviewed 2026-08-17.
#
# This does NOT permit gradients on surfaces. If a gradient ever appears as a
# card or section background here, remove this line and fix the gradient.
harsh gradient
